@startuml TCU-NAD System Context – Linux IDS
!theme plain
skinparam defaultFontSize 11
skinparam actorStyle awesome

title TCU / NAD Deployment – System Context Diagram

' === External Actors ===
actor "SOC / Fleet\nOperator" as SOC
actor "ML Engineer" as MLEng
actor "Vehicle Driver" as Driver

' === Cloud ===
cloud "OEM Cloud Backend" as Cloud {
    component "OTA Server\n(Model Updates)" as OTA_Server
    component "SIEM / Telemetry\n(Alert Ingestion)" as SIEM
    component "ML Platform\n(Retraining)" as MLPlat
}

' === Cellular Network ===
node "LTE / 5G\nNetwork" as Cellular #LightYellow

' === Vehicle ===
package "Vehicle" as Vehicle {

    package "CAN Bus Network" as CAN_Net {
        node "CAN HS Bus\n(500 kbps)" as CAN_HS #LightYellow
        node "Engine ECU" as ECU_ENG #LightCyan
        node "Transmission\nECU" as ECU_TRANS #LightCyan
        node "ADAS ECU" as ECU_ADAS #LightCyan
        node "Body Control\nModule" as BCM #LightCyan
        node "OBD-II Port" as OBD #Orange
    }

    node "TCU / NAD" as TCU #LightGreen {
        component "Linux (Yocto / AGL)" as Linux
        component "IDS Service\n(tiny-can-ids)" as IDS #PaleGreen
        component "SocketCAN\n(can0)" as SCAN
        component "OTA Agent" as OTA_Agent
        component "MQTT Client" as MQTT_C
        component "CAN-to-Ethernet\nBridge" as CAN_ETH
    }

    node "Instrument\nCluster / HMI" as HMI #LightCyan
    node "Central\nGateway" as GW #Plum
}

' === Data flows ===
ECU_ENG --> CAN_HS
ECU_TRANS --> CAN_HS
ECU_ADAS --> CAN_HS
BCM --> CAN_HS
OBD --> CAN_HS : <<attack vector>>

CAN_HS --> GW : All frames
GW --> SCAN : Forwarded\nframes
SCAN --> IDS : CAN frames\nvia SocketCAN

IDS --> MQTT_C : Alert events\n(JSON)
IDS --> Linux : syslog /\njournald
MQTT_C --> Cellular : Publish\nalerts
Cellular --> SIEM : Alert data

OTA_Server --> Cellular : Model update\npackage
Cellular --> OTA_Agent : Download\nupdate
OTA_Agent --> IDS : Hot-swap\nmodel file

IDS --> CAN_ETH : Stream to\nbackend (opt.)
CAN_ETH --> Cellular : CAN-over-IP

IDS --> GW : Alert frame\n(CAN TX)
GW --> HMI : Warning\ndisplay

SOC --> SIEM : Monitor\nalerts
MLEng --> MLPlat : Train &\npublish model
MLPlat --> OTA_Server : New model\nartifact
Driver --> HMI : Observes\nalert

note right of TCU
  **Hardware examples:**
  Qualcomm SA515M (Cortex-A7)
  NXP i.MX8 (Cortex-A53)
  Cinterion ELS62 (LTE Cat 1)
  RAM: 256 MB – 1 GB
  Flash: 256 MB – 4 GB
end note

note bottom of IDS
  **Model formats supported:**
  • .tflite (TensorFlow Lite)
  • .onnx (ONNX Runtime)
  • .so (compiled C library)
  • .pkl (Python scikit-learn)
  Inference: < 1 ms
end note

note left of OBD
  **Threats detected:**
  DoS flooding
  Fuzzy frame injection
  Gear/RPM spoofing
  Replay attacks
end note

note right of Cloud
  **Cloud loop:**
  1. IDS detects anomaly → alert
  2. SIEM correlates across fleet
  3. ML platform retrains model
  4. OTA pushes updated model
end note

@enduml